course: dictionary
lesson: 13057
title: Fearsome
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Fearsome means very frightening. Something fearsome is big, strong or dangerous, so it makes you feel scared. «The fearsome shark swam closer to the boat.» A shark is dangerous, and fearsome tells you how frightening it is.
explain: Fearsome can also mean very impressive or hard to deal with. People might say a team has a fearsome reputation when other teams are scared to play against it. «The team had a fearsome reputation for winning.» This means the team is very strong, not that it is scary to look at.
explain: To check a word, put your meaning into the sentence. «The dragon had fearsome teeth.» Does "The dragon had very frightening teeth" make sense? Yes, so fearsome fits here.
fact: Fearsome is an adjective, so it describes a noun, like a fearsome shark or a fearsome warrior.
fact: «Fearsome» means very frightening to look at or meet, or very hard to deal with.
fact: The forms are fearsome, more fearsome and most fearsome.
fact: «Fearsome» is often used for monsters, animals, warriors and sports teams.
fact: Do not mix up fearsome with fearful. Fearful means you feel scared, but fearsome means the thing itself is scary.
exercise: «The fearsome shark swam closer to the boat.» What does fearsome mean here? | *Very frightening | Very sleepy | Very tiny and harmless | Very quiet
exercise: «The team had a fearsome reputation, and other teams were scared to play them.» What does fearsome suggest? | Very small | Very wet | *Very impressive and hard to beat | Very funny
exercise: Find and copy the word that means very frightening: «The fearsome dragon had sharp claws and a long tail.» | claws | *fearsome | dragon | tail
test: «The fearsome warrior raised his sword.» Which word tells you the warrior is scary? | Warrior | Sword | Raised | *Fearsome
test: Choose the right form: «The lion was ___ than the cat.» | Fearsome | most fearsome | *more fearsome | Fearsomer
exam: «Her fearsome stare made the whole class go quiet.» What does fearsome mean? | Very sleepy | Very funny | Very kind and gentle | *Very frightening or hard to deal with
